<Base title="For teachers" description="How the Clear Physics lessons are built, and how to use them.">
  <h1>For teachers</h1>
  <p>
    These lessons are for classes that learn physics in English as a second language.
  </p>

  <h2>Language</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Short sentences and common words, when possible.</li>
    <li>The exam key words are kept. Each lesson lists its key words, with a simple meaning in the <a href={url('key-words/')}>Key words</a> list.</li>
    <li>Figures, animations and simulations support the text.</li>
    <li>In calculations, the data is set apart: <em>Given</em> and <em>Find</em>.</li>
    <li>Command words (<em>state, describe, explain…</em>) have their own <a href={url('key-words/#command-words')}>list</a>, and a lesson in Unit 18.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Lesson structure</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Goals and key words</strong>, with the syllabus codes.</li>
    <li><strong>Starter</strong> (5 min): a question or a short demonstration.</li>
    <li><strong>Learn</strong>: the explanation, with worked examples.</li>
    <li><strong>Do</strong>: a practical or an on-screen activity.</li>
    <li><strong>Practice</strong>: online questions with new numbers each time and hints for typical mistakes.</li>
    <li><strong>Exit ticket</strong>: a short quiz to check learning.</li>
    <li><strong>Homework</strong> and <strong>teacher notes</strong> (timing, common mistakes and other advice).</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Your scheme of work</h2>
  <p>
    The lessons follow the order of the <a href={url('course/')}>course</a>, but each lesson works on its own.
    You can use them inside your own scheme of work.
    To see which syllabus topic each unit covers, and the sources we use, read <a href={url('syllabus/')}>Syllabus and sources</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Printable worksheets</h2>
  <p>
    Make <a href={url('worksheets/')}>printable worksheets</a> from the practice topics: choose the topics and levels,
    and print a different version for each student, with new numbers. The answers (and, if you want, the worked solutions)
    for every version are printed at the end. Keep the code: the same code always gives the same sheets.
  </p>
</Base>
